<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lakshmana Sena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1178–1206</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lakshmana Sena was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-dynasty">Sena dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> who reigned from about 1178 to about 1206. A patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> literature, he kept at his court the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayadeva">Jayadeva</a>, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gita-govinda">Gita Govinda</a>. Around 1204 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiyar-khalji">Bakhtiyar Khalji</a> surprised him at Nadia, and he fled to eastern Bengal, where his dynasty survived for some decades while the west fell to Muslim rule.</p></div>
